```cedar
// Close a work order only at MAIN, and only with a granted approval
// (APPR) for the same work order, made by someone other than the agent.
permit (
  principal,
  action == AOB::Action::"close_workorder",
  resource
)
when {
  context.input.site_id == "MAIN" &&
  context has approval &&
  context.approval.status == PGI::ApprovalStatus::"APPR" &&
  context.approval.wonum == context.input.wonum &&
  context.approval.site_id == context.input.site_id &&
  context.approval.approver != principal
};

// List work orders only when the request explicitly targets site MAIN.
permit (
  principal,
  action == AOB::Action::"list_workorders",
  resource
)
when {
  context.input has site_id &&
  context.input.site_id has typeChoice0 &&
  context.input.site_id.typeChoice0 == "MAIN"
};
```

I took "granted approval" to mean status `APPR`. The other statuses, including the waiting one (`WAPPR`), do not count.

The `close_workorder` tool description says "Do not use for work orders at site MAIN". I followed your instruction to allow closing at MAIN, so that policy is only as permissive as the tool itself lets it be.
